Align venus virtgpu blob sizes to 16KiB for Apple Silicon hosts.

macOS hosts map host-visible blobs into the guest address window with
hv_vm_map(), which works on 16KiB (Apple page size) granularity. The guest
drm_mm packs blobs at their size alignment, so 4KiB-aligned sizes land
blobs at offsets the host cannot map and venus fails with
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY. Rounding the size up before creation makes
every blob offset 16KiB-aligned (same approach as UTM's guest Mesa
packages); the mmap length uses the same rounded size, keeping the guest
kernel's vm_size == vram_node.size check happy.

Equivalent to the runtime LD_PRELOAD shim in bobrvm's
tools/venus_align_shim.c, done properly at the source level.

--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_virtgpu.c	2026-07-30 12:17:21
+++ src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_virtgpu.c	2026-07-30 12:17:21
@@ -1313,6 +1313,12 @@
    VkExternalMemoryHandleTypeFlags external_handles,
    struct vn_renderer_bo **out_bo)
 {
+   /* Apple Silicon hosts (bobrvm/UTM) map host-visible blobs with 16KiB
+    * granularity; round sizes up so drm_mm places every blob at a
+    * host-mappable offset. Harmless over-allocation elsewhere.
+    */
+   size = align64(size, 16384);
+
    struct virtgpu *gpu = (struct virtgpu *)renderer;
    const uint32_t blob_flags =
       virtgpu_bo_blob_flags(gpu, flags, external_handles);
@@ -1392,6 +1398,9 @@
 static struct vn_renderer_shmem *
 virtgpu_shmem_create(struct vn_renderer *renderer, size_t size)
 {
+   /* See virtgpu_bo_create_from_device_memory: 16KiB host pages. */
+   size = align64(size, 16384);
+
    struct virtgpu *gpu = (struct virtgpu *)renderer;
 
